{"name":"Bright Idea","hex":"#ecbe63","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bright","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Emitting much light; visually dazzling; luminous, lucent, radiant.","Of light: brilliant, intense."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Brightness, glow.\n\n Glory, splendour.","Brightness, glow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bright"},{"term":"idea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An abstract archetype of a given thing, compared to which real-life examples are seen as imperfect approximations; pure essence, as opposed to actual examples. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The conception of someone or something as representing a perfect example; an ideal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/idea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bright Idea","blocks":[{"text":"Bright Idea is the debut studio album of American power pop band Orson. Originally self-released in 2005, it was released commercially on May 29, 2006 in the UK and internationally on June 13, 2006."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/75/BrightIdea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bright_Idea","wikidata":"Q3644686"},{"title":"Idea","blocks":[{"text":"An idea is the result of thought. Although the word is used in common usage, in philosophy, ideas can also be mental representational images of some object. Many philosophers have considered ideas to be a fundamental ontological category of being. The capacity to create and understand the meaning of ideas is considered to be an essential and defining feature of human beings."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4a/Plato-raphael.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idea","wikidata":"Q131841"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/common